      "pos": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "data": {
        "text": "Clock test: three rows, the same test picture and the same Deflection Yoke in each. Only what drives the Yoke's H coil input is different.\nA, top row. Scan Sync DOWN into the Yoke. Expect: the picture stands still, sheared the same way every picture.\nB, middle row. A free-running Fundamental LFO saw at 60.5 Hz into the same input. Expect: the picture rolls, because 60.5 Hz is not the picture rate (59.94 Hz).\nC, bottom row. The same LFO, but Scan Sync TOP goes into its RESET input, which restarts the saw at the top of every picture. Expect: the picture stands still.\nScan Sync LINES and the Yoke LINES are both 240.\nKnown: DOWN through the Yoke is unsteady in the top rows."
      }
    }
  ],
